# Tessera Discover section. Copy to .env.local and fill in the keys you have.
# Every source degrades gracefully: without a key its tab is disabled and the
# rest of the site is unaffected.
#
# NASA, Wallhaven (SFW) and Reddit all work with no key at lower rate limits.
# Only Unsplash, Pexels and Pixabay strictly need one.

# Unsplash: https://unsplash.com/oauth/applications  (use the Access Key)
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# Pexels: https://www.pexels.com/api/
PEXELS_API_KEY=

# Pixabay: https://pixabay.com/api/docs/
PIXABAY_API_KEY=

# Wallhaven (optional, only needed for mature content): https://wallhaven.cc/settings/account
WALLHAVEN_API_KEY=

# NASA needs no key (the images library API is open), so there is nothing to set.

# Reddit works without an app via the public JSON API. Setting a client
# id/secret from a "web app" at https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps raises the
# rate limit. The user agent is used with or without an app; Reddit rejects
# generic ones, so set it if you deploy anywhere public.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=web:tesseera:v1.0 (by /u/your-reddit-username)
